<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dahod</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Dohad</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dahod is a city in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, near the borders of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madhya-pradesh">Madhya Pradesh</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasthan">Rajasthan</a>, and the headquarters of Dahod district, created in 1997 from part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/panchmahal-district">Panchmahal district</a>. It lies on old trade routes between Gujarat and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malwa">Malwa</a>. The Mughal emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aurangzeb">Aurangzeb</a> was born there in 1618.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dahod.jpg" alt="Dahod" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gazal world · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jilla_Panchayat_Bhawan_Dahod.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
